modified: distractors sampled, intent names reformatted, packaged as System One requests.

=====================================================================================================================
bench/data/wide_items.jsonl (source repository only)
The wide-choice validation items: 20 BANKING77 and 20 CLINC150 utterances from the train splits. This file is not in
the wheel or the sdist: the package ships no CLINC150 data. The file's first row (_meta) records the sources,
revisions, sha256s, licences and attribution; bench/wide_items.py builds it.

BANKING77, training split: the attribution and the CC-BY-4.0 licence are in the BANKING77 section above, but this file
reads a different source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/legacy-datasets/banking77 (the Hub's parquet copy of
PolyAI/banking77) at revision f54121560de48f2852f90be299010d1d6dc612ec (data/train-00000-of-00001.parquet).
Used: train utterances and intent names, unmodified; sampled.

CLINC150, training split (config plus: 150 intents and oos)
Stefan Larson, Anish Mahendran, Joseph J. Peper, Christopher Clarke, Andrew Lee, Parker Hill, Jonathan K. Kummerfeld,
Kevin Leach, Michael A. Laurenzano, Lingjia Tang and Jason Mars, "An Evaluation Dataset for Intent Classification and
Out-of-Scope Prediction", EMNLP-IJCNLP 2019, https://github.com/clinc/oos-eval.
Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/clinc/clinc_oos at revision 155b9c710419136e17307b80d0a13e68cd46b4ec
        (plus/train-00000-of-00001.parquet)
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported (CC-BY-3.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
Used: train utterances and intent names (150 intents and oos), unmodified; sampled.

modified (both sources): 20 intents sampled (seed 0) and one utterance of each; each item packaged with the
dataset's full intent list and a 10-option control (the gold plus 9 sampled distractors, shuffled).
